WEBVTT

00:05.260 --> 00:07.150
All students still on school grounds,

00:06.120 --> 00:06.160
Nanyou
High School

00:07.150 --> 00:09.340
please make your way home promptly.

00:09.340 --> 00:10.640
I repeat.

00:10.640 --> 00:12.560
The school day is over.

00:12.560 --> 00:14.380
All students still on school grounds,

00:14.380 --> 00:16.560
please make your way home promptly.

00:16.460 --> 00:19.420
Staff Office

00:16.560 --> 00:19.520
Yes. Yes. I'm terribly sorry.

00:19.520 --> 00:22.430
Yes, of course. We are dealing with this as best we can.

00:23.210 --> 00:29.950
Absolutely. We will prevent any future recurrences, so please overlook this incident.

00:29.950 --> 00:32.110
Thank you. Goodbye.

00:34.760 --> 00:37.920
Our neighbors are complaining daily now, and it's all getting too much.

00:37.920 --> 00:40.870
Whatever happened to keeping an eye on our students, Sasaki?

00:40.870 --> 00:44.550
Oh, yes, well... we're doing everything we can.

00:44.550 --> 00:47.430
And on top of all this, the
class outings are coming up.

00:47.430 --> 00:49.470
I'm counting on you to set them straight.

00:49.470 --> 00:50.800
I'm sorry for allowing this to happen.

00:52.280 --> 00:55.000
Yes, this is Nanyou High School.

00:55.000 --> 00:56.520
Yes. <i>What ?!</i>

00:57.140 --> 00:59.210
I sincerely apologize... Yes...

00:59.210 --> 01:00.970
Those fucking punks...

01:06.590 --> 01:09.000
Itou!

01:09.740 --> 01:12.370
Whatcha doing down there?

01:12.370 --> 01:14.120
Planning on playing hooky?

01:14.840 --> 01:17.020
You're so uncultured.

01:17.020 --> 01:19.160
I'm enjoying the autumn air.

01:19.740 --> 01:21.070
How out of character!

01:21.070 --> 01:22.630
Mitsuhashi!

01:22.630 --> 01:25.420
I wouldn't go to school
right now if I were you.

01:25.420 --> 01:27.370
Huh? Why not?

01:27.700 --> 01:29.270
Ouch!

01:29.990 --> 01:31.420
What was that for?!

01:31.420 --> 01:33.610
What do you call that
shambles of a uniform?!

01:33.610 --> 01:35.560
Have you even read
the school's rulebook?!

01:35.560 --> 01:37.070
And what’s with this mop?

01:37.070 --> 01:38.760
Go get a buzz cut this instant!

01:38.500 --> 01:40.000
You gotta be kidding...

01:38.760 --> 01:42.170
Don’t talk back! Now, go back home!

01:39.650 --> 01:42.940
He’s confiscating all short-cut blazers.

01:42.940 --> 01:44.840
What’s brought this on, all of a sudden?

01:44.840 --> 01:46.920
Who knows. He looks pretty full-on.

01:46.920 --> 01:50.290
And I only bought this the other day!

01:50.650 --> 01:51.640
So, we bunking?

01:51.640 --> 01:54.910
No. We'll overcome this wall of adversity and...

02:08.340 --> 02:11.040
Whoa! I knew they'd
think of something.

02:10.950 --> 02:15.420
Starting  today,  I'll!!

02:11.200 --> 02:15.420
Presented by Saizen-Yabai

02:15.500 --> 02:19.880
And Yet, You're Going to Kyoto!

02:25.440 --> 02:27.780
Excuse me, but it's time to close the gates now.

02:27.780 --> 02:29.960
But the two biggest
troublemakers aren't here yet...

02:29.960 --> 02:30.410
Huh?

02:30.750 --> 02:32.950
Mitsuhashi and Itou.

02:32.950 --> 02:36.990
If those two aren't dealt with first, no one else will listen to us.

02:36.990 --> 02:39.470
Those two loose cannons...

02:39.980 --> 02:41.880
Wait a minute... Maybe they...

02:42.420 --> 02:43.320
Asai.

02:43.320 --> 02:43.810
Yes.

02:43.810 --> 02:44.810
Asakura.

02:44.810 --> 02:45.340
Yes.

02:45.340 --> 02:46.520
Ando.

02:46.520 --> 02:47.230
Yes.

02:47.230 --> 02:48.150
Ishida.

02:48.150 --> 02:49.150
'Sup!

02:49.760 --> 02:51.740
Itou?! Mitsuhashi?!

02:51.740 --> 02:54.090
Wh-What are you doing here, Mr. Sasaki?

02:54.090 --> 02:55.770
Administering discipline!

02:55.770 --> 02:56.930
Show yourselves!

02:56.930 --> 02:57.800
Over here!

02:58.550 --> 02:59.830
Sure enough...

03:01.370 --> 03:03.320
How did you get in?!

03:03.320 --> 03:04.420
How?

03:04.420 --> 03:06.280
We walked in through the gate, of course!

03:06.280 --> 03:09.490
Don't take me for a fool.
Where are your uniforms?!

03:09.490 --> 03:13.090
We were helping out this old
woman who fell into a ditch...

03:13.090 --> 03:14.620
...and our uniforms got dirty, so—

03:14.620 --> 03:18.990
Oh, there’s no need to heap praise on us. We were just being good Samaritans.

03:19.830 --> 03:21.920
What a load of bull...

03:21.920 --> 03:24.910
Okay then, what about your hairdos?!

03:26.020 --> 03:28.810
I don’t remember saying these hairstyles were allowed in school.

03:29.010 --> 03:29.770
Ow...

03:33.090 --> 03:34.860
Oh, what's this?

03:34.860 --> 03:36.430
Why have you raised your hand?

03:36.990 --> 03:38.390
Bastard...

03:38.390 --> 03:42.350
Your expression tells me you wanna pick a fight with your teacher...

03:42.690 --> 03:44.710
Is that right, Mitsuhashi?

03:49.740 --> 03:53.240
That's just how my face always looks. I didn't mean nothing by it.

03:53.240 --> 03:57.440
What's this? You two don't put up a fight at all... do you?!

03:59.660 --> 04:00.900
Fucking bastard...

04:00.900 --> 04:02.930
Listen carefully.

04:02.930 --> 04:06.130
If you two don't get haircuts, we won't be taking you on the field trip.

04:06.800 --> 04:10.400
And that doesn't just go for these two! It applies to anyone who ignores school rules!

04:10.400 --> 04:11.680
Don't forget it.

04:11.680 --> 04:14.260
Ouch...

04:16.780 --> 04:20.680
That asshole! I wouldn't go to Kyoto, even if he got down on his knees and begged!

04:20.680 --> 04:22.720
What? You're not serious, are you, Three?

04:22.720 --> 04:23.770
Course I am!

04:23.770 --> 04:27.730
It's no big deal. All you have to do is dye your hair black for the trip. Let's go sort it now.

04:27.730 --> 04:31.700
Hmph! Who'd want to rock a bland look like that? Right, Itou?

04:31.700 --> 04:35.910
You said it! I don't wanna go if it means we have to humor that bastard!

04:36.220 --> 04:41.110
Then, that means you two won't be in our class trip photo.

04:42.210 --> 04:46.420
Which means you won't have that memory in your yearbook.

04:47.440 --> 04:48.950
You're a sly shrew, aren't you?

04:48.950 --> 04:53.800
Whatever. There's <i>no way
we're going on that field trip!</i>

04:53.800 --> 04:55.000
You with me, Itou?

04:55.000 --> 04:56.390
Right on!

04:56.720 --> 04:58.220
Yeah, exactly!

04:58.220 --> 05:01.240
It looks like we'll be able to meet up in Eigamura,

05:01.240 --> 05:02.530
so should we?

05:03.490 --> 05:04.600
You'd better come.

05:04.600 --> 05:06.280
I’m looking forward to it already!

05:06.280 --> 05:08.720
Okay, good night.

05:13.660 --> 05:15.310
What a predicament...

05:23.920 --> 05:27.360
Nozomi

05:23.920 --> 05:27.360
Kodama

05:23.920 --> 05:27.360
Hikari

05:23.920 --> 05:27.360
Shin

05:23.920 --> 05:27.360
Oosaka

05:24.400 --> 05:26.770
Seriously, who decided on a 9:30 start?

05:26.770 --> 05:29.160
It took me two hours to get here!

05:27.460 --> 05:29.790
Please form two lines, people.

05:29.160 --> 05:31.070
Who <i>does that? I mean, <i>come on!</i></i>

05:29.790 --> 05:32.900
Your group leaders will do a head count!

05:31.690 --> 05:33.840
Oh well, not much we can do.

05:33.840 --> 05:37.070
Riko, there’s no point waiting for them.

05:37.730 --> 05:39.650
I wonder if they really decided not to show...

05:39.650 --> 05:42.950
It's a huge weight off my shoulders.
You've done well, Mr. Sasaki.

05:42.950 --> 05:44.060
I knew I could count on you.

05:44.060 --> 05:47.710
Those boys would've dragged our school's reputation through the mud if they'd come!

05:47.710 --> 05:49.270
Sorry I'm late!

05:54.000 --> 05:55.930
Good morning!

05:56.940 --> 05:58.100
Who are you?

05:58.100 --> 05:59.830
Stop joking around, Teach.

05:59.830 --> 06:02.080
It's Itou. Itou Shinji.

06:02.080 --> 06:03.160
Say what?

06:03.160 --> 06:04.790
Itou... you say?

06:05.400 --> 06:07.870
Is my hairstyle acceptable now?

06:10.600 --> 06:14.700
Oh, I see. It's Itou. How pathetic.

06:14.700 --> 06:17.210
So you wanted to go that badly?

06:17.720 --> 06:20.720
I guess we've got no choice but to take you with us.

06:20.720 --> 06:22.170
Where's Mitsuhashi, anyway?

06:25.880 --> 06:27.460
Bento

06:26.000 --> 06:26.080
Oolong Tea

06:30.960 --> 06:33.180
What the hell was that about?

06:34.280 --> 06:35.590
What's wrong?

06:37.990 --> 06:41.220
Oh, um, nothing! I just need to use the restroom!

06:41.220 --> 06:43.420
But the train's about to leave!

06:43.420 --> 06:44.750
I’ll be right back!

06:50.620 --> 06:54.840
For Chrissake... now it looks like I've pissed myself!

06:54.840 --> 06:56.910
What's going on here?

07:05.010 --> 07:05.970
What the...

07:08.270 --> 07:08.890
They've gone!

07:08.890 --> 07:11.890
Attention all passengers. Please be advised...

07:11.890 --> 07:13.940
that the Nozomi Bullet Train service to Hakata...

07:12.230 --> 07:14.560
Mr. Sasaki's not back yet.

07:13.940 --> 07:15.730
will shortly be departing from Platform 18.

07:15.730 --> 07:16.600
Oh, heck!

07:19.320 --> 07:21.780
Hey! Wait for me!

07:26.120 --> 07:27.690
Hey! Stop struggling!

07:27.690 --> 07:30.350
No, it's not what you think! Please let go of me!

07:36.250 --> 07:40.090
Don't let it get you down, Riko.

07:40.090 --> 07:43.470
Yeah, just forget about Mitsuhashi while we're on this trip.

07:43.470 --> 07:46.220
It's not like I even give a rat's ass what he does.

07:46.220 --> 07:47.510
Oopsy-daisy.

07:47.510 --> 07:48.470
What?

07:48.470 --> 07:50.060
You don't give a rat's ass?

07:50.060 --> 07:52.140
That's not a nice thing to say.

07:52.140 --> 07:53.180
Three?!

07:55.870 --> 07:56.610
Huh?

07:57.940 --> 07:59.360
Mitsuhashi!

07:59.360 --> 08:00.700
What happened to Sasaki?

08:01.070 --> 08:03.010
I took him out of the equation.

08:03.010 --> 08:03.660
What?

08:03.660 --> 08:04.950
Let go of me!

08:12.250 --> 08:15.370
You're pulling my leg!
Is it really you, Itou-kun?

08:15.370 --> 08:17.270
It's like he's a completely different person!

08:17.270 --> 08:19.710
This look suits you way better!

08:19.710 --> 08:22.030
Why don't you just keep it like this?

08:22.680 --> 08:23.720
You think I should?

08:24.040 --> 08:26.290
Hey, let's get a photo of me and you!

08:26.290 --> 08:27.890
Let me jump in too!

08:27.890 --> 08:28.890
Okay, say "cheese"!

08:28.890 --> 08:32.190
Even so, he looks like a real geek!

08:32.190 --> 08:34.470
Oh yeah! He <i>so does!</i>

08:35.100 --> 08:38.150
Have you got any <i>weird collections at home?</i>

08:38.600 --> 08:40.780
Maybe he even grows his own moss balls!

08:40.780 --> 08:43.580
Oh wow! Gross!

08:43.600 --> 08:47.430
Truth is...

08:43.640 --> 08:47.430
he
does
grow
his
own
moss
balls

08:47.860 --> 08:50.330
Maybe he even likes to watch Internet porn!

08:50.310 --> 08:54.230
Truth is...

08:50.350 --> 08:54.230
he
does
mess
around
with
PCs

08:54.460 --> 08:55.360
Mitsuhashi!

08:57.250 --> 08:59.210
Now, look here, Mitsuhashi!

09:00.380 --> 09:01.820
You're so irritating.

09:01.820 --> 09:04.170
I was trying to get some sleep.

09:04.170 --> 09:06.090
I think I'll go get myself a drink of water.

09:12.220 --> 09:12.840
My bad.

09:16.270 --> 09:17.680
What the hell are you doing?!

09:18.810 --> 09:21.650
Why, of all places, is Imai on this train?

09:22.820 --> 09:25.820
Oh? What's this? Ignoring me?

09:26.530 --> 09:28.370
Hey! Hold up a sec.

09:31.030 --> 09:33.290
What school are you from, jackass?

09:33.290 --> 09:36.000
Tanigawa kicked the back of my knee!

09:36.000 --> 09:38.030
You think you can get away with disrespecting...

09:38.030 --> 09:41.120
the big cheeses of Beni High?! Well, brat?!

09:41.120 --> 09:43.090
"B-Brat"?!

09:43.090 --> 09:46.430
Do you even know who you're messing with, huh?!

09:46.430 --> 09:47.340
Huh?

09:47.340 --> 09:50.760
Imai, doesn’t this guy look a helluva lot like that dipshit, Mitsuhashi?

09:50.760 --> 09:53.260
Oh, now that you mention it, he's a spitting image of him.

09:53.260 --> 09:55.140
This is a great opportunity, Imai.

09:55.140 --> 09:57.680
We can take out our
frustrations on this guy instead.

09:57.680 --> 09:59.100
Works for me.

09:59.100 --> 10:00.200
Hey, bonehead—

10:00.200 --> 10:01.480
Ouch!

10:01.480 --> 10:02.900
What the hell are you doing, you brat?!

10:02.900 --> 10:06.560
You numskulls. You have no right to call me...

10:07.230 --> 10:08.480
a "brat"!

10:08.480 --> 10:11.440
M-Mitsuhashi?!

10:13.330 --> 10:17.120
Right then. What are you bozos gonna do now?

10:17.120 --> 10:20.700
I, Mitsu-fucking-hashi, won't just let you off the hook after you attacked me—

10:22.810 --> 10:26.660
Wait, that means... It can't be... That guy behind you is Itou?!

10:27.670 --> 10:29.800
What are you supposed to be? A '70s folk singer?!

10:29.800 --> 10:31.300
You look ridiculous!

10:32.710 --> 10:36.130
I can't breathe! I'm seriously gonna die of laughter!

10:37.850 --> 10:39.210
You jerk-offs...

10:39.210 --> 10:42.140
If you don't quit that cackling, we'll kick your faces in!

10:44.900 --> 10:45.940
Oh, man!

10:48.770 --> 10:50.160
What's he doing?

10:51.140 --> 10:52.780
What are you guys doing out here?

10:53.110 --> 10:55.450
I thought I told you two not to start any trouble.

10:55.450 --> 10:56.500
It's not like that.

10:57.120 --> 10:59.190
These guys are our friends.

10:59.450 --> 11:00.840
Is this true?

11:00.840 --> 11:02.730
Uh, I guess so...

11:03.460 --> 11:05.000
Hurry back to your seats.

11:05.000 --> 11:06.340
Yes, sir!

11:13.760 --> 11:15.410
What are you assholes looking at?

11:15.410 --> 11:18.770
Nitwit, nitwit, nitwit...

11:20.520 --> 11:21.960
You bastards! Don't fuck with—

11:21.960 --> 11:23.190
Hey, Teach!

11:31.450 --> 11:33.010
Damn it, Imai, you son of a bitch!

11:33.010 --> 11:34.280
Hey, Teach!

11:34.910 --> 11:37.200
Come on, Itou, do something!

11:37.200 --> 11:39.730
Why are you crying out for Itou, you loser?

11:39.730 --> 11:43.580
Yell at us again and I'll fetch your teacher!

11:43.580 --> 11:45.570
What're you gonna do now, Mitsuhashi?

11:45.570 --> 11:48.790
You can't fight back now, can you? You dickless wonder!

11:48.790 --> 11:51.080
Hey, don’t bug me. We're having a moment here.

11:54.760 --> 11:56.470
What are you doing, Imai?

11:57.340 --> 11:59.220
R-Riko...

11:59.220 --> 12:01.060
Th-This isn't what it looks like...

12:02.270 --> 12:03.150
Imai.

12:03.150 --> 12:04.600
Y-Yes?

12:05.480 --> 12:07.820
Please stop picking on Three.

12:13.850 --> 12:17.240
I actually feel sorry for him...

12:28.000 --> 12:31.170
Cheer up, Imai.

12:37.300 --> 12:38.300
Tanigawa.

12:38.300 --> 12:39.070
Yes?

12:39.640 --> 12:43.180
Am I the bad guy in all this? Am I the bully?

12:43.180 --> 12:44.640
Absolutely not!

12:44.640 --> 12:46.940
You're the victim in this scenario!

12:46.940 --> 12:49.130
It's Riko who just doesn't get it.

12:49.130 --> 12:51.360
Don't badmouth my Riko.

12:52.190 --> 12:53.030
Whoops, sorry.

12:53.030 --> 12:54.820
Mitsuhashi's the one to blame...

12:54.820 --> 12:57.370
That brain-dead brat! I'll never...

12:57.370 --> 13:00.200
...let you get away with this, Imai, you horse's ass!

13:00.200 --> 13:03.870
Keep acting cocky. I won't let you forget this.

13:08.120 --> 13:10.760
Mishima. This is Mishima.

13:10.760 --> 13:13.750
The train arriving at the platform is the Nozomi service to Hakata.

13:13.750 --> 13:17.090
Please be advised that these carriages are reserved and not for the general public.

13:25.230 --> 13:27.890
The teachers won't find us out here.

13:27.890 --> 13:29.570
How about we settle this, Imai?

13:30.230 --> 13:31.610
That was the plan.

13:31.610 --> 13:33.530
Payback's a bitch.

13:33.530 --> 13:36.400
Sounds peachy, but there’s
definitely not enough time for this.

13:36.400 --> 13:38.370
The train'll leave without us.

13:38.370 --> 13:39.780
Don't worry.

13:39.780 --> 13:42.080
You'll be out for the count in the blink of an eye.

13:50.000 --> 13:52.850
Fuck this! Is dodging all you can muster, Mitsuhashi?

13:53.380 --> 13:56.210
He must be shit-scared of getting caught red-handed by his teachers.

14:00.300 --> 14:01.430
But wait a tick...

14:01.430 --> 14:04.850
Why would Mitsuhashi pick a fight with me if he can’t lay a finger on me?

14:08.930 --> 14:10.270
That's what he's doing!

14:10.270 --> 14:13.110
He plans to escape by jumping on the train at the last second and leaving us stranded!

14:17.440 --> 14:21.040
While he was dodging, he edged closer to the train doors.

14:21.040 --> 14:23.780
All right. I'll play along and then, at the last moment,

14:23.780 --> 14:25.910
I'll turn the tables on you, Mitsuhashi!

14:25.910 --> 14:27.740
What's wrong? Come at me!

14:27.740 --> 14:31.210
Stay put. Stare him down until the
moment the train starts leaving.

14:31.210 --> 14:33.290
Okay, then I'll come after <i>you instead!</i>

14:33.580 --> 14:34.240
Idiot.

14:36.380 --> 14:36.970
I won!

14:37.670 --> 14:39.180
Now! Run, Tanigawa!

14:40.130 --> 14:40.970
Come on! Hurry up!

14:44.430 --> 14:45.890
I did it! I finally won!

14:45.890 --> 14:46.970
I beat that bastard, Mitsuhashi!

14:46.970 --> 14:49.600
I'm the winner!

14:49.600 --> 14:51.640
Imai, you did it!

14:52.060 --> 14:54.760
Shit-for-brains! Loo-hoo-sers!

14:54.760 --> 14:56.470
Go back home to Tokyo,

14:56.470 --> 14:59.290
you dumbasses!

15:10.950 --> 15:12.960
Hey, they just went...

15:12.960 --> 15:14.010
Yeah...

15:14.590 --> 15:16.670
Imai! You've finally done it!

15:16.670 --> 15:17.840
Thank you, Tanigawa!

15:17.840 --> 15:20.590
This moment has touched me to my very core!

15:20.590 --> 15:23.450
Imai! I'm so happy!

15:24.130 --> 15:26.000
The next stop is the final stop:

15:26.000 --> 15:28.390
Tokyo. Tokyo.

15:28.390 --> 15:29.810
Tokyo?!

15:33.440 --> 15:35.350
Isn't that a little bit<i> too cruel?</i>

15:35.350 --> 15:37.640
I didn't think they'd actually get on it...

15:37.640 --> 15:38.810
I feel sorry for him.

15:38.810 --> 15:40.700
Hey, what are you guys doing?!

15:41.160 --> 15:42.990
The train's about to leave!

15:42.990 --> 15:44.150
Hurry!

15:44.150 --> 15:45.250
Right!

15:45.860 --> 15:46.920
This door.

16:06.000 --> 16:06.040
Nanyou High School

16:18.360 --> 16:20.610
Heaven! I'm in heaven.

16:20.610 --> 16:22.980
A nice, spacious hot spring after a delicious meal.

16:22.980 --> 16:25.320
Field trips are pretty awesome!

16:25.320 --> 16:29.120
Now, if only there were geishas serving me drinks and feeding me daimonji-yaki...

16:25.320 --> 16:31.130
Translation Note: Daimonji-yaki is a Kyoto festival. Mitsuhashi mistakes "yaki" for food, as several cooked meats end with this suffix.

16:29.120 --> 16:31.130
That'd be the life!

16:31.960 --> 16:33.830
U-Uh, Mitsuhashi,

16:33.830 --> 16:36.460
Daimonji-yaki isn't food...

16:36.460 --> 16:40.130
Even a foreigner wouldn't stick their foot in their mouth that bad.

16:40.130 --> 16:43.090
Wh-What? Didn't you realize it was a pun?

16:43.090 --> 16:45.840
Well, well. Sounds like you're having fun.

16:45.840 --> 16:49.000
"I wouldn't go to Kyoto, even if he got down on his knees and begged!"

16:49.340 --> 16:51.730
Shut up! Quit bringing up ancient history...

16:51.080 --> 16:51.130
Smart

16:51.730 --> 16:54.180
and rubbing it in my face!

16:54.180 --> 16:55.680
I'm coming to get you!

16:55.680 --> 16:57.180
Whoa, Mitsuhashi! Get down!

16:59.390 --> 17:00.650
Hot!

17:01.700 --> 17:03.220
Oh, please, no...

17:03.690 --> 17:05.320
Thank you!

17:05.320 --> 17:07.370
You pervert!

17:15.070 --> 17:15.110
Kyoto

17:20.670 --> 17:24.130
Tonight's gonna be another energetic one...

17:24.130 --> 17:26.930
on Rumina Mayumi's "Big Night Course"!

17:27.540 --> 17:27.580
Squid

17:33.300 --> 17:37.100
Stowing away in a truck with Kyoto plates sounded like a good idea at the time,

17:37.100 --> 17:39.090
but I didn't realize it was a refrigerator truck!

17:39.090 --> 17:41.100
Imai... I'm gonna take a nap...

17:41.100 --> 17:42.520
You idiot! Don’t fall asleep, Tanigawa!

17:42.770 --> 17:45.330
If you fall asleep, you'll die! Tanigawa!

17:47.900 --> 17:49.070
Imai!

17:49.070 --> 17:50.990
If you fall asleep, you'll die!

17:50.990 --> 17:52.580
Imai!

17:54.620 --> 17:56.490
Tanigawa! I said don't fall asleep!

17:56.490 --> 17:58.630
You gutless dork!

18:10.930 --> 18:13.090
It's time to form up into your groups!

18:13.090 --> 18:16.830
Don't wander off and please follow the specified route!

18:16.830 --> 18:19.800
This is such a drag.

18:18.390 --> 18:19.800
Hey, you two over there.

18:19.800 --> 18:20.860
Huh?

18:20.860 --> 18:22.810
If you don't come with us,

18:22.810 --> 18:25.970
they'll single me out for blame because I'm the group leader!

18:25.970 --> 18:28.570
The four of us are gonna walk around together as a group.

18:29.320 --> 18:30.730
So Ryou's our leader, huh?

18:30.730 --> 18:32.660
When was this decided, huh?

18:32.660 --> 18:35.450
One of the times you two ditched class and ran off.

18:35.450 --> 18:36.680
I veto this.

18:36.680 --> 18:37.490
Three!

18:37.490 --> 18:40.630
Come on, let Ryou have his moment in the sun.

18:43.190 --> 18:43.870
Welcome!

18:47.470 --> 18:49.920
I mean, seriously...

18:49.920 --> 18:53.130
What's so great about visiting these temples, anyway?

18:53.130 --> 18:56.400
Why did you even come to Kyoto, Mitsuhashi?

18:59.850 --> 19:01.430
Wow! This is it!

19:01.430 --> 19:03.770
This is the famous Kiyomizu shrine stage!

19:03.770 --> 19:05.430
What's that? Is someone going to sing?

19:05.430 --> 19:06.780
Hold up a second!

19:08.150 --> 19:11.860
We need a little history lesson before we go inside.

19:11.860 --> 19:13.820
Now, take out your guidebooks!

19:13.820 --> 19:15.290
Oh, come off it, Ryou...

19:15.290 --> 19:19.370
"Kiyomizu Temple, formerly known as Seisuiji, was constructed during the Heian period...

19:19.370 --> 19:24.870
on the orders of General
Sakanoue no Tamuramaro..."

19:21.570 --> 19:22.690
Three!

19:25.420 --> 19:29.010
Wowee! We're really high up!

19:32.170 --> 19:34.260
Oh! I want to get my fortune told!

19:34.260 --> 19:34.970
Me too.

19:34.970 --> 19:38.100
You idiots, don't bother.
It's a waste of money.

19:41.550 --> 19:43.530
Number 21, huh?

19:45.690 --> 19:46.810
Excuse me,

19:46.810 --> 19:48.480
number 21, pleas—

19:48.480 --> 19:49.860
Number 13, please.

19:49.860 --> 19:51.950
And make it snappy, Granddad.

19:52.940 --> 19:56.620
It'd be awesome if I got a "Great Fortune" message and met a really cute girl!

19:56.620 --> 19:58.040
Hold your horses, assholes.

19:58.040 --> 19:59.200
Huh?

19:59.200 --> 20:02.030
Are you gonna cut in line
without even saying hello?

20:02.660 --> 20:03.750
What'd you say?!

20:03.750 --> 20:05.420
Hey, dork-features,

20:05.420 --> 20:07.500
have you got any idea who you're talking to?

20:07.500 --> 20:09.580
Who the hell are you calling dork-features?!

20:09.580 --> 20:10.970
Hey, dork!

20:10.970 --> 20:12.580
What'cha doing over here?

20:12.580 --> 20:15.560
Can't you even buy a goddamn fortune by yourself?!

20:18.140 --> 20:20.600
H-He's blond.

20:20.600 --> 20:22.600
O-Oh shit...

20:23.270 --> 20:24.210
Let's get outta here.

20:24.210 --> 20:24.890
Right behind you.

20:24.890 --> 20:26.900
Hey, wait, you fuckers!

20:26.900 --> 20:30.110
With your geeky mug, no one's gonna take you seriously, no matter how hard you act.

20:30.110 --> 20:31.240
You're so hopeless.

20:37.410 --> 20:39.160
Hey, Three, let's go stand in that line!

20:39.160 --> 20:40.160
What?

20:40.160 --> 20:42.240
But just look at how long that line is...

20:42.240 --> 20:44.290
The waterfall grants you three wishes!

20:44.290 --> 20:45.790
Let's go! Come on!

20:44.980 --> 20:45.790
Hey, hey!

20:45.790 --> 20:49.050
Have fun. I'm gonna go find the restroom.

20:49.050 --> 20:51.090
Let's see... Oh, there it is!

20:52.840 --> 20:55.510
Kyou's hotel is...

20:55.510 --> 20:56.730
Yo.

20:59.970 --> 21:02.090
We've been waiting for you, dorkface.

21:02.090 --> 21:04.050
Where'd your blond friend go?

21:04.890 --> 21:06.510
You got something to say to him?

21:06.510 --> 21:08.020
We've got something to say to you.

21:08.020 --> 21:10.980
Acting all hard 'cause your friend protects you.

21:11.360 --> 21:13.530
What's wrong? You look worried.

21:13.530 --> 21:15.610
We'll give you a few seconds if you want to cry out:

21:15.610 --> 21:18.330
"Save me, blondie!"

21:18.330 --> 21:20.030
Hey, douchebags...

21:20.030 --> 21:23.290
Judging a book by its cover can land you in serious trouble.

21:28.340 --> 21:30.820
Did you piss a river, Itou?

21:30.820 --> 21:32.340
My bad, my bad.

21:52.360 --> 21:54.360
As I gaze out at the pebbles,

21:54.360 --> 21:56.820
they start to look like they're flowing, like a river.

21:56.820 --> 21:57.970
It's incredible.

21:58.490 --> 22:01.160
That is the first step to enlightenment.

22:01.160 --> 22:06.310
You will soon detach yourself from the distractions of this world and clear your mind.

22:06.310 --> 22:08.460
Hey, Itou!

22:09.210 --> 22:11.000
It's not a big deal, but man...

22:11.000 --> 22:12.960
this yard is hard to walk through!

22:12.960 --> 22:15.760
I keep getting grit in my shoes.

22:16.430 --> 22:19.550
They shoulda laid down turf. Then, it wouldn't kick up so much dust.

22:20.090 --> 22:23.270
So anyway, Itou, where the hell's this famous garden meant to be?

22:23.270 --> 22:26.230
Well, you're sitting in it.

22:26.230 --> 22:27.720
This place?!

22:27.720 --> 22:30.940
Why on earth is this stupid
moss-covered rock famous?

22:30.940 --> 22:33.070
M-Mitsuhashi...

22:39.990 --> 22:42.690
Hey! What the hell do you
teenagers think you're doing?!

22:42.910 --> 22:44.700
You idiots. It's only me.

22:45.660 --> 22:47.910
Oh, it's just Mura.

22:47.910 --> 22:48.420
Here.

22:48.420 --> 22:49.950
Oh, thanks.

22:49.950 --> 22:51.660
Huh?

22:51.660 --> 22:52.880
What happened to your faces?

22:53.210 --> 22:55.080
O-Oh, nothing important.

22:55.080 --> 22:56.960
You got your asses handed to you in Kiyomizu, didn't you?

22:56.960 --> 22:57.930
Shut up!

22:57.930 --> 22:59.120
What the hell...

22:59.120 --> 23:01.170
Don't embarrass us all the way out here in Kyoto.

23:01.170 --> 23:03.970
But it was this really strong geeky kid.

23:03.970 --> 23:06.390
Maybe we should get Nakano to set him straight.

23:06.390 --> 23:07.430
You dunce.

23:07.430 --> 23:10.930
All hell would break loose if we got Nakano involved.

23:10.930 --> 23:12.210
Yeah, exactly.

23:12.210 --> 23:14.570
There's no stopping him once he's unleashed.

23:14.570 --> 23:17.230
Fuck's sake! I'm still pissed about it.

23:17.230 --> 23:19.760
Well, if we see him again, I'll take care of him.

23:19.760 --> 23:22.030
We're counting on you, Mura!

23:25.320 --> 23:26.570
Excuse me.

23:26.570 --> 23:29.290
Has a package been delivered for a Mitsuhashi or Itou?

23:29.290 --> 23:30.370
From Chiba?

23:30.370 --> 23:32.300
Oh, from Nanyou High School.

23:33.290 --> 23:34.620
Yes, it has arrived.

23:34.620 --> 23:35.460
This is it, yes?

23:35.710 --> 23:37.790
Oh, that's the ticket!

23:37.790 --> 23:39.060
Thank you.

23:57.440 --> 23:58.650
We're here.

23:58.650 --> 24:01.110
We finally made it to Kyoto, Tanigawa.

24:01.110 --> 24:03.990
It was a long and grueling trip, wasn't it, Imai?

24:03.990 --> 24:06.370
Tanigawa, let's go find Mitsuhashi,

24:06.370 --> 24:07.740
and exact our revenge.

24:07.740 --> 24:09.200
Let's do it, Imai!

24:09.200 --> 24:12.740
Tanigawa! I'm so emotional right now!

24:18.880 --> 24:22.840
Tanigawa... Since when was Kyoto by the sea?

24:22.840 --> 24:25.630
Well, it's not far from a sea, but...

24:25.630 --> 24:28.730
this looks like the Sea of Japan...

24:25.870 --> 24:25.910
Welcome to
aaaaaaa Wakkanai  !

24:47.280 --> 24:49.910
Ah, what a great feeling!

24:49.910 --> 24:51.830
Everyone's looking at me differently now.

24:51.830 --> 24:53.170
Hey, you guys!

24:54.120 --> 24:55.820
What's with those getups?

24:55.820 --> 24:58.300
If the teachers see you, they'll send you straight back home!

24:58.300 --> 25:00.360
I'd like to see them try to send us all the way home.

25:00.360 --> 25:02.720
Not gonna happen. Right, Itou?

25:04.010 --> 25:07.840
Itou? Little Itou? Where are you?!

25:07.840 --> 25:08.970
Three!

25:11.640 --> 25:14.530
He'll mess up everything if he's around.

25:20.480 --> 25:23.400
Say, Kyouko, what's your boyfriend like?

25:23.400 --> 25:25.470
He goes to Nanyou High, doesn't he?

25:25.990 --> 25:29.570
He's tall, really kind, and handsome to boot!

25:29.570 --> 25:31.510
Gimme a slice of that!

25:31.950 --> 25:34.750
Well, hello, ladies. Looks like you’re having a good time.

25:34.750 --> 25:37.660
How about we join you?

25:37.660 --> 25:39.670
We could use some ladies in this sausage fest.

25:40.040 --> 25:42.120
Hey, shorty,

25:42.120 --> 25:44.290
how about we go grab ourselves some tea?

25:44.290 --> 25:46.000
Hey, don't. Don't touch me.

25:46.000 --> 25:47.430
It's okay, isn't it?!

25:48.140 --> 25:49.840
Get your hands off of her.

25:49.840 --> 25:50.930
She told you not to touch her.

25:52.970 --> 25:55.100
You're annoying the fuck out of us.

25:55.100 --> 25:57.020
What was that, you whore?

25:57.020 --> 25:58.840
How dare you talk to us like that?

25:58.840 --> 26:01.110
Hold up. Let's forget this crazy bitch.

26:01.110 --> 26:02.400
Let's go, guys.

26:02.400 --> 26:03.630
The hell you lookin' at?!

26:03.630 --> 26:05.070
This ain't a show!

26:06.030 --> 26:07.400
Yow! Ice cold.

26:07.400 --> 26:09.420
It's been ages since we've seen Kyouko get mad!

26:09.420 --> 26:11.320
That's why she's the boss of Seiran Girls' Academy!

26:11.320 --> 26:13.330
Kyou!

26:13.330 --> 26:14.530
Itou!

26:14.530 --> 26:16.080
Sorry I'm late.

26:16.080 --> 26:18.700
I had real trouble losing Mitsuhashi.

26:18.700 --> 26:21.540
You just missed these awful men who were bothering us...

26:22.540 --> 26:23.580
Who were they?!

26:23.580 --> 26:26.080
I don't know, but they were really scary.

26:26.080 --> 26:27.380
So that's Kyouko's boyfriend!

26:27.380 --> 26:29.300
What a hunk!

26:29.760 --> 26:31.470
Later, girls.

26:31.470 --> 26:32.710
Excuse us, ladies.

26:32.710 --> 26:35.930
Little Itou! Where’d you go?

26:35.930 --> 26:37.230
Little Ito—

26:40.860 --> 26:44.190
Just kidding!

26:44.190 --> 26:46.950
Stop it, Itou!

26:49.690 --> 26:52.070
When the hell did he meet up with Kyou?!

26:52.070 --> 26:55.250
Itou, you bastard. Cheating on me behind my back!

26:55.250 --> 26:57.110
Hey, look at the leaves over there.

26:57.110 --> 26:58.940
Wow, they're so pretty.

27:01.330 --> 27:02.830
Who did that?!

27:02.830 --> 27:04.380
Are you okay, Itou?!

27:04.670 --> 27:05.790
Ouch...

27:06.090 --> 27:08.850
Pain, pain, go away!

27:06.540 --> 27:09.460
What happened, Itou?! Oh, who's this?

27:08.850 --> 27:12.380
Oh wow! I'm suddenly all better! The pain's vanished!

27:09.460 --> 27:10.590
It's Kyouko!

27:10.590 --> 27:11.930
I didn't realize you were in Kyoto too!

27:11.920 --> 27:13.960
You never told me!

27:12.380 --> 27:14.920
Oh, Itou, you're so funny.

27:14.930 --> 27:16.590
Kyou's funny too!

27:17.890 --> 27:19.420
Dammit!

27:20.220 --> 27:22.020
Ow, ow, ow!

27:24.270 --> 27:25.810
This so isn't my day...

27:25.810 --> 27:29.310
We made it... We finally made it, Tanigawa.

27:29.310 --> 27:32.190
We've sure traveled a long way, haven't we, Imai?

27:32.190 --> 27:34.640
We're gonna find that bastard Mitsuhashi, Tanigawa.

27:34.640 --> 27:36.290
Imai.

27:36.290 --> 27:38.030
Where have you been?

27:38.030 --> 27:40.250
The teachers are seriously pissed.

27:40.790 --> 27:42.620
I don't give a fuck about that.

27:42.620 --> 27:44.800
We're hunting down Mitsuhashi. Find Mitsuhashi!

27:44.800 --> 27:48.400
Forget about Mitsuhashi. We're in Kyoto now.

27:48.400 --> 27:50.760
Why don't you come hang out with us instead?

27:50.760 --> 27:52.470
Who are the chicks?

27:52.470 --> 27:54.390
Oh, I'll introduce you.

27:54.760 --> 27:57.670
We met them a little earlier. They're from an all girls' school in Saitama.

27:57.800 --> 27:59.060
I'm Ai!

27:59.060 --> 28:00.130
I'm Yumi!

28:00.130 --> 28:01.180
I'm Raiko!

28:01.180 --> 28:02.950
How about it? Let's hang out together!

28:02.950 --> 28:04.510
No thanks.

28:04.510 --> 28:06.950
I only have eyes for Riko.

28:08.230 --> 28:10.420
What about you, Tanigawa?

28:10.420 --> 28:12.780
You birdbrains! Tanigawa's not gonna leave my side—

28:12.780 --> 28:15.200
I'll tag along if you don't mind!

28:15.200 --> 28:17.690
Hi! I'm Tanigawa! Nice to meet you all!

28:18.410 --> 28:20.820
Hey, what happened to your face?

28:20.820 --> 28:23.250
Oh, I just got back from a little excursion to the Sea of Japan.

28:23.250 --> 28:25.360
Ah, I want to go there!

28:25.360 --> 28:26.910
You chickenshit!

28:29.710 --> 28:31.290
What are you doing, asshole?!

28:31.550 --> 28:32.460
What'd you say?

28:32.460 --> 28:34.010
I'm not in a good mood...

28:34.340 --> 28:36.340
Hey, good timing.

28:36.340 --> 28:37.890
We're not in a good mood either.

28:37.890 --> 28:38.960
So we doing this or what?

28:38.960 --> 28:40.100
Say what?

28:40.100 --> 28:43.050
There are lots of 'em. I'm screwed.

28:46.590 --> 28:50.310
Huh? He didn't put up much of a fight for such a big guy.

28:50.310 --> 28:51.810
He's just a moron.

28:52.670 --> 28:54.150
What the hell did you say?!

28:54.570 --> 28:56.990
Oh, fuck it, I didn't get any sleep.

28:57.570 --> 28:58.610
Dammit!

28:59.450 --> 29:02.360
You! Look me in the eye and start fighting—

29:02.360 --> 29:03.700
Hey, knock it off!

29:03.700 --> 29:06.080
Ganging up on one guy like that...

29:06.080 --> 29:08.670
People like you disgust me the most.

29:08.670 --> 29:09.880
Itou...

29:09.880 --> 29:11.340
Kyou, get out of here for a bit.

29:11.340 --> 29:12.200
This won't take long.

29:12.200 --> 29:13.210
But...

29:13.210 --> 29:15.930
It's okay. I'm only going to stop them. I promise.

29:17.130 --> 29:18.390
Promise me.

29:19.560 --> 29:21.210
What do you want?

29:21.210 --> 29:22.270
Huh?

29:23.510 --> 29:26.610
Aren't you the guys from Kiyomizu Temple?

29:28.230 --> 29:31.060
D-Don't tell me you're the geek from yesterday!

29:31.060 --> 29:32.680
He looks like a completely different person.

29:32.680 --> 29:35.190
Hmph. So he's not a nerd, after all.

29:35.190 --> 29:37.500
He's just some batshit crazy thug.

29:38.240 --> 29:41.400
Didn't I teach you only yesterday not to judge a book by its cover?

29:42.280 --> 29:44.700
You saved me some time and trouble finding you.

29:44.700 --> 29:47.500
This is payback for what you did to my friends.

29:47.500 --> 29:50.760
Today'll be different, you son of a bitch.

29:51.250 --> 29:55.210
It's at times like this that I wish Mitsuhashi was here...

29:55.210 --> 29:56.570
Brace yourself!

29:58.110 --> 29:59.020
Ow!

29:59.880 --> 30:01.000
Who did that?!

30:08.730 --> 30:09.650
That's freakin' gross!

30:09.650 --> 30:11.110
Mitsuhashi!

30:12.440 --> 30:13.960
You're cold, Itou!

30:13.960 --> 30:15.540
Having all this fun on your own!

30:17.610 --> 30:19.110
Let me jump in.

30:19.110 --> 30:21.030
Stay back, Mitsuhashi.

30:21.030 --> 30:23.280
What the hell? They're friends?

30:23.280 --> 30:24.990
Th-They are.

30:24.990 --> 30:27.000
He looks like a real headcase.

30:27.000 --> 30:29.660
And what's with the outfit?

30:29.400 --> 30:29.530
Truth

30:29.660 --> 30:32.420
I got it at the store! Don’t I look cool?

30:32.420 --> 30:33.670
Not even a little.

30:33.670 --> 30:34.360
Oh, rats.

30:34.360 --> 30:35.170
Hey.

30:35.500 --> 30:37.630
Where the hell are you two from?

30:37.630 --> 30:38.930
Up there!

30:38.930 --> 30:40.540
You wanna die or something?!

30:40.540 --> 30:42.380
I'm asking what school you're from.

30:42.760 --> 30:45.430
If it's really that important to you, I’ll tell you.

30:45.430 --> 30:46.600
Chiba.

30:46.600 --> 30:49.050
There isn't a single person in Chiba who doesn't know me.

30:51.020 --> 30:53.340
How pathetic! Chiba!

30:53.340 --> 30:55.680
So you have juice in Chiba, huh?

30:55.680 --> 30:57.450
Where the hell are you guys from then?!

30:57.450 --> 30:59.660
We're from Ibaraki!

31:02.370 --> 31:05.390
You're hicks? You gotta be kidding me!

31:05.390 --> 31:07.560
I ain't taking that from some asswipe from Chiba!

31:07.560 --> 31:08.860
All you've got is farmland!

31:08.860 --> 31:11.820
I fucking hate it when people call our prefecture "Chibaraki"!

31:11.820 --> 31:13.540
Like you can talk.

31:13.540 --> 31:15.240
Do you even have a convention center?

31:15.240 --> 31:16.250
How about an airport?

31:16.250 --> 31:18.080
What about Disneyland?

31:18.080 --> 31:19.090
You've got mush for brains!

31:19.090 --> 31:22.300
They call it "Tokyo Disneyland" and "Tokyo Airport,"

31:22.300 --> 31:24.510
'cause saying "Chiba" would be lame as hell!

31:24.510 --> 31:28.580
Okay, then tell me: Is there even anything worth bragging about in Ibaraki?

31:28.580 --> 31:31.970
You dumbo! We grow the best fermented soy beans!

31:34.440 --> 31:37.270
You're bragging about soy beans?! What losers!

31:37.270 --> 31:38.900
We just dug our own graves.

31:38.900 --> 31:42.860
Itou! Let's leave these hayseeds alone and get back to civilization.

31:43.070 --> 31:44.310
Don't you run away from us!

31:57.000 --> 31:59.670
Hey! What's going on over there?!

31:59.670 --> 32:01.850
Shit! L-Let's scram!

32:05.630 --> 32:07.640
Jeez, they're fast.

32:07.640 --> 32:10.690
Oh man, the set's completely ruined.

32:14.060 --> 32:16.930
Anyway, let's find this kid's teacher.

32:16.930 --> 32:19.310
This is gonna cost a fortune to fix up...

32:24.030 --> 32:26.030
Dammit, this is pissing me off.

32:26.530 --> 32:29.990
Don't sweat it so much. It's better to leave 'em well alone.

32:29.990 --> 32:32.500
But Nakano's gonna yell at us again.

32:33.330 --> 32:35.460
What? You told Nakano about this?

32:35.460 --> 32:36.970
Well...

32:36.970 --> 32:39.280
The bruises were pretty obvious.

32:39.280 --> 32:39.790
Yo.

32:39.790 --> 32:40.600
Huh?!

32:44.470 --> 32:47.890
You guys lost again, didn't you?

32:47.890 --> 32:50.760
N-Not at all! Right, guys?

32:50.760 --> 32:51.940
R-Right.

32:51.940 --> 32:53.810
Hm? So?

32:53.810 --> 32:57.980
Where are the stupid bitches who stood up to us?

32:57.980 --> 32:59.030
Have you found them?

32:59.030 --> 33:00.640
Oh, that?

33:00.640 --> 33:01.940
Well, you know...

33:01.940 --> 33:04.240
Yeah, you don't have to worry about that anymore!

33:04.240 --> 33:06.220
Oh? What does that mean?

33:06.220 --> 33:06.700
I mean...

33:07.070 --> 33:11.740
There’s no need to get your hands dirty, is there, Nakano?

33:11.740 --> 33:12.830
Exactly.

33:12.830 --> 33:15.250
So it's all sorted now.

33:15.620 --> 33:17.130
Sure is!

33:24.220 --> 33:26.260
What the hell is this?

33:26.630 --> 33:28.210
W-Wait a minute, Nakano!

33:30.680 --> 33:34.440
Now, tell me. Why are you
bullshitting little ol' me, huh?

33:34.440 --> 33:36.900
N-No, well...

33:37.810 --> 33:40.420
What the hell does "it's all sorted now" mean anyway?

33:40.420 --> 33:42.190
N-Nakano, calm down.

33:42.190 --> 33:46.200
Mura. Do you think I'm stupid?

33:46.200 --> 33:47.490
No, it's not like that.

33:47.490 --> 33:49.360
What is it "like" then?

33:49.360 --> 33:53.450
I came here, pumped with adrenaline, to fight some brainless dickheads, and now what?

33:53.450 --> 33:54.320
B-But look...

33:54.320 --> 33:55.420
"But" nothing!

33:55.830 --> 33:57.660
Find those punks this instant.

33:57.660 --> 34:01.880
Or I might have to fuck someone else up.

34:03.790 --> 34:05.340
G-Gotcha.

34:05.240 --> 34:05.280
Uzumasu Eigamura

34:06.380 --> 34:08.750
Let's have some fun today!

34:08.750 --> 34:09.760
Yeah!

34:09.760 --> 34:12.060
I had some green tea ice cream!

34:15.010 --> 34:16.810
Hey, Riko, what's that?

34:16.810 --> 34:19.320
Yatsuhashi! I'm gonna eat it later at the hotel!

34:20.640 --> 34:21.460
No! Don't do that!

34:21.460 --> 34:22.900
C'mon!

34:22.900 --> 34:24.810
H-Hold it, Three!

34:25.280 --> 34:26.870
Stop that! Give them back!

34:28.570 --> 34:31.120
He ate half in one second flat...

34:32.240 --> 34:33.740
I've got heartburn.

34:33.740 --> 34:35.580
Riko! Give me some tea!

34:35.580 --> 34:37.410
I don't have any!

34:37.410 --> 34:39.460
Itou! Got any tea?

34:39.460 --> 34:40.410
Nope.

34:40.410 --> 34:41.300
Dang.

34:42.120 --> 34:42.800
Oh.

34:45.090 --> 34:46.010
Yo! Tanigawa!

34:46.750 --> 34:49.180
Give me a swig of that!

34:53.180 --> 34:53.970
All gone.

34:53.970 --> 34:55.230
What?

34:56.430 --> 34:58.110
Why, that little...

34:58.770 --> 35:01.220
Tanigawa! That was low!

35:02.310 --> 35:06.440
You cheap bastard! You sneak! Devil!

35:06.440 --> 35:09.070
Nakano, that's him.

35:30.260 --> 35:31.700
Three! Are you okay?

35:31.700 --> 35:32.220
Mitsuhashi!

35:32.670 --> 35:33.630
What's going on?

35:33.630 --> 35:34.680
Nothing!

35:34.680 --> 35:38.640
This is what happens when you pick a fight with us.

35:38.640 --> 35:40.140
Bastards...

35:40.140 --> 35:42.360
Don't mess with us, you scumbags!

35:43.270 --> 35:44.400
What did you just throw?

35:52.240 --> 35:53.990
Nanyou High School, huh?

35:53.990 --> 35:55.790
I won't forget that.

35:57.020 --> 35:57.060
Reserved for Nanyou High School

36:00.700 --> 36:03.050
Goddamn midget.

36:03.540 --> 36:05.680
And yet, you're still gonna drink it...

36:05.680 --> 36:07.620
Have you no shame?

36:13.220 --> 36:15.600
I won't let you get away with this, shortass.

36:23.730 --> 36:25.480
Mitsuhashi! Itou!

36:25.480 --> 36:27.900
I won't allow you to cause any more trouble!

36:28.270 --> 36:31.620
We can't just wave the white flag, Ryou.

36:32.990 --> 36:34.700
We're counting on you to be our lookout.

36:34.700 --> 36:36.450
Hey! Wait, you guys!

36:36.450 --> 36:38.500
I'm supposed to be in charge here!

36:38.500 --> 36:39.830
I'm in charge!

36:39.830 --> 36:40.660
Hey!

36:40.660 --> 36:41.410
Listen!

36:45.250 --> 36:46.790
Yes, that's it.

36:46.790 --> 36:49.040
From Ibaraki. They wear blue.

36:49.040 --> 36:51.550
I have an item that belongs to them.

36:51.550 --> 36:53.130
Oh? Not staying there?

36:53.130 --> 36:54.760
I see. Thanks.

36:55.670 --> 36:57.250
The next hotel is this one.

36:57.250 --> 37:00.520
It looks like it'll be impossible to find them like this...

37:00.520 --> 37:02.510
Yes, hello? Is this the East Hotel?

37:02.510 --> 37:04.520
Are there any students from Ibaraki staying there?

37:04.520 --> 37:05.630
With blue uniforms?

37:06.190 --> 37:07.440
What, they’re there?

37:07.440 --> 37:09.560
And where are they now?

37:09.560 --> 37:10.440
Thanks!

37:13.980 --> 37:15.280
Found you.

37:15.280 --> 37:18.160
They're hanging out in the Shinkyogoku district.

37:24.580 --> 37:27.540
Tonight's the last night of our
thrills-and-spills field trip, huh?

37:27.540 --> 37:30.690
Tomorrow, it'll be back to
boring reality with a bump.

37:30.690 --> 37:31.500
What a downer.

37:31.500 --> 37:33.960
That's not necessarily true, Mura.

37:33.960 --> 37:37.220
Once we get back, we can start looking for the school that kid belongs to.

37:37.220 --> 37:39.920
Huh? You still have it in for those guys?

37:39.920 --> 37:41.350
Of course.

37:41.350 --> 37:44.690
I etched the name of their school into my brain.

37:48.940 --> 37:51.640
Check out that punch! Worth writing home about, huh?!

37:51.640 --> 37:53.150
Wow, awesome!

37:55.190 --> 37:57.440
Hey, I'm still in the middle of this.

37:58.660 --> 38:00.940
I'm not done with it yet—

38:07.580 --> 38:08.690
This is fun.

38:08.690 --> 38:09.700
What the hell are you doing?!

38:15.090 --> 38:18.170
What are you doing, interrupting someone's fun like that?

38:18.170 --> 38:19.450
Are you listening?

38:19.450 --> 38:20.590
Nakano, that's enough.

38:21.390 --> 38:22.970
What's that, Mura?

38:22.970 --> 38:24.560
You wanna fight me now?

38:24.890 --> 38:27.310
Why do you always have to be like this?

38:27.310 --> 38:29.230
I don’t plan on fighting you.

38:29.230 --> 38:31.270
You're shaking.

38:31.270 --> 38:32.940
Are you <i>that afraid of me?</i>

38:32.940 --> 38:37.910
I'm just worried that you'll get your ass kicked one day.

38:38.410 --> 38:41.860
And who'd be kicking my ass exactly?

38:46.990 --> 38:48.210
Which bastard threw that?!

38:51.460 --> 38:52.960
It's those fuckers!

38:57.000 --> 38:58.930
I came here to return something.

38:58.930 --> 39:03.390
Oh, I was wondering who it was.
It’s the Yatsuhashi kid.

39:03.390 --> 39:05.280
You've made it real easy for me.

39:05.280 --> 39:06.890
Don't do it, Nakano...

39:06.890 --> 39:08.930
There's no stopping us now.

39:08.930 --> 39:11.980
It took some serious effort to find you.

39:18.290 --> 39:20.530
Hey, where did the guys go?

39:23.870 --> 39:28.230
To make sure they don't get caught, I have to eat all of their food!

39:31.380 --> 39:33.160
Ew, gross!

39:41.030 --> 39:41.640
Damn you!

39:44.870 --> 39:46.140
This is fun, isn't it?!

39:51.940 --> 39:55.100
Goddamn hobbit... Zipping around like that...

39:56.690 --> 39:59.450
It's been a while since someone's hit me.

39:59.450 --> 40:01.800
Then, maybe you'd like a kick too!

40:01.800 --> 40:03.250
As if!

40:07.490 --> 40:10.650
Having a fast punch doesn't mean shit.

40:10.650 --> 40:12.990
Then, try this on for size!

40:18.610 --> 40:20.300
Not bad, blondie.

40:20.300 --> 40:25.350
The world's a big place. There's a lot you don't know, shortass.

40:26.170 --> 40:30.890
Hey. Your friend's pretty dumb...

40:30.890 --> 40:31.810
Why's that?

40:32.210 --> 40:37.040
Nakano's not only the strongest, he's also the fastest by a long shot.

40:37.040 --> 40:40.840
Is there anything between your ears?
Mitsuhashi can beat anyone, anytime.

40:40.840 --> 40:43.520
Oh, you're rather cocksure.

40:43.790 --> 40:49.000
Of course. Mitsuhashi won't lose to a guy like him.

40:49.000 --> 40:54.000
Oh well. Having psychotic friends isn't exactly easy on us...

40:54.970 --> 40:56.460
Yeah, guess so...

40:56.460 --> 41:00.050
You assholes! Are you the kids that messed up our friend?!

41:00.050 --> 41:02.800
This is bad. Those guys are from the arcade.

41:02.800 --> 41:04.310
Nakano, we're going!

41:04.310 --> 41:05.260
What the—

41:05.260 --> 41:06.250
Come on!

41:06.970 --> 41:08.220
Don't let 'em get away!

41:08.220 --> 41:09.180
Okay!

41:09.770 --> 41:10.910
Wh-What's this now?

41:10.910 --> 41:12.690
M-Mitsuhashi! Run!

41:13.890 --> 41:15.290
Hey, get back here!

41:15.290 --> 41:17.110
We didn't do shit!

41:21.990 --> 41:28.690
Damn. I won't feel any better unless I find Mitsuhashi, and land a punch on his mush.

41:28.690 --> 41:31.590
Not to mention, if we don't make up for the two days we lost,

41:31.590 --> 41:33.810
the teachers are gonna blow their lids.

41:33.810 --> 41:35.450
Mitsuhashi, that bastard...

41:35.450 --> 41:37.390
Move it! Outta the way!

41:38.870 --> 41:41.050
Don’t just stand there, blocking the sidewalk, you assholes!

41:43.270 --> 41:45.150
Th-That was Mitsuhashi!

41:47.870 --> 41:50.890
M-Mitsuhashi! I've been looking all over for you!

41:50.890 --> 41:53.720
Oh, Imai! How's it going?

41:53.720 --> 41:59.710
Shut up! You have no idea what I've been through because of you!

41:59.710 --> 42:00.960
We have to settle this right now!

42:00.960 --> 42:03.330
Settle this?! I don’t have time for that right now!

42:03.330 --> 42:06.410
Uh, how about you meet me at the Kiyomizu stage tomorrow?

42:06.410 --> 42:08.210
We'll slug it out there!

42:08.910 --> 42:10.490
Okay, gotcha!

42:10.490 --> 42:11.850
You'd better be there!

42:12.250 --> 42:13.270
I will!

42:13.990 --> 42:15.750
Hey, get back here!

42:16.970 --> 42:18.310
Tanigawa?

42:18.310 --> 42:19.030
Yes?

42:19.030 --> 42:22.410
Do you know where the Kiyomizu stage is?

42:22.410 --> 42:23.450
Totally!

42:23.450 --> 42:24.090
All right.

42:36.730 --> 42:38.030
What was with that gang?

42:38.030 --> 42:38.870
Who knows...

42:38.870 --> 42:41.730
Why are <i>we the ones being chased?</i>

42:46.360 --> 42:48.030
What is it with these guys?

42:48.030 --> 42:51.770
Man, what are the odds of them running to the same place we did?

42:51.770 --> 42:54.790
We picked a great place to bump heads.

42:54.790 --> 42:58.320
Hey, blondie, why'd ya run?

42:58.670 --> 43:00.790
You bastards were the ones that ran away,

43:00.790 --> 43:02.960
and left us in that mess.

43:02.960 --> 43:05.300
This time, I'll finish you off.

43:05.300 --> 43:07.230
Oh! There they are! Down there!

43:07.230 --> 43:09.620
All right, let's flank 'em. Don't let 'em get away!

43:09.620 --> 43:10.460
Gotcha!

43:15.180 --> 43:17.710
Man, how annoying.

43:17.990 --> 43:21.900
Yo, blondie, how about we call a temporary truce?

43:21.900 --> 43:23.230
A truce...

43:23.230 --> 43:28.200
Let's team up to finish off this gang, then we can settle our differences. Okay?

43:29.730 --> 43:33.550
Don't do it, Mitsuhashi.
We don't owe this guy a thing.

43:33.550 --> 43:35.250
I know that.

43:35.250 --> 43:35.990
So why?

43:35.990 --> 43:36.780
Even so—

43:38.090 --> 43:39.030
Mitsuhashi!

43:41.920 --> 43:42.870
Mitsuhashi!

43:47.890 --> 43:48.880
Motherfu—

43:50.990 --> 43:52.130
Stop it!

43:55.900 --> 43:59.100
Mitsuhashi! Mitsuhashi!

44:04.750 --> 44:06.410
That was horrible!

44:09.310 --> 44:11.850
He's out cold.

44:11.850 --> 44:15.740
Who's next?! Who wants to go lie down in a hospital bed?

44:15.740 --> 44:17.010
Don't fuck with us.

44:17.010 --> 44:20.080
We've got weapons, you know!
And how many of us do you think there are?

44:20.080 --> 44:22.410
Sounds like fun. Come on then!

44:22.410 --> 44:28.120
I hate to lose, so you'd better be prepared to die if you come at me.

44:28.120 --> 44:28.970
Good!

44:28.970 --> 44:30.130
Hold onto your hat!

44:30.130 --> 44:31.230
Here we come.

44:31.230 --> 44:32.290
Hold on.

44:34.590 --> 44:37.950
Sorry, guys, but you gotta let me fight him.

44:39.090 --> 44:41.330
What was that? Just butt out!

44:41.330 --> 44:45.190
He hurt my best friend. I’ll be the one to finish him off.

44:45.190 --> 44:46.470
Like we give a shit.

44:46.470 --> 44:50.430
Hold up, this might be a laugh. Why don't you do us the honor?

44:50.430 --> 44:51.710
How do you feel about it?

44:51.710 --> 44:56.730
It doesn't matter. I don't care who my opponent is.

44:58.310 --> 45:00.390
And so the show begins.

45:00.390 --> 45:02.710
We'll sit back and lap it up.

45:04.450 --> 45:08.190
Wait, Itou. I'll beat him to a pulp.

45:08.190 --> 45:09.180
I got this.

45:09.180 --> 45:10.380
Here I come, Spikes!

45:19.010 --> 45:22.050
What?! They still aren't back yet?!

45:22.670 --> 45:24.380
So they disappeared earlier...

45:24.380 --> 45:26.370
Maybe they're out fighting again...

45:26.370 --> 45:28.860
I really hope they don't get hurt.

45:29.290 --> 45:30.770
They'll be fine, Riko.

45:31.990 --> 45:32.750
Yeah.

45:32.750 --> 45:34.370
I'll call back a little later.

45:35.190 --> 45:36.050
Bye.

45:38.450 --> 45:41.620
Itou... I hope you're not doing anything reckless...

45:56.570 --> 45:58.550
Cocksucker!

46:06.610 --> 46:09.970
What's wrong? You seem a little slower now.

46:09.970 --> 46:12.330
You irritating bastard!

46:14.930 --> 46:15.810
Wow.

46:15.810 --> 46:18.170
This is more fun than watching professional wrestling.

46:18.170 --> 46:19.740
Keep it up, Spikey!

46:20.690 --> 46:25.000
What's with this guy?! Things'd go a lot easier for him if he just stayed down.

46:26.730 --> 46:30.950
None of your moves are doing the business.

46:31.910 --> 46:33.910
Shut the hell up, you son of a bitch!

46:37.790 --> 46:42.830
I never lose! I hate losing! So just lie down and die!

46:44.990 --> 46:49.100
Give me a sec, Itou...
I'll kick his ass for you...

46:49.100 --> 46:51.220
Shut up! Just shut the fuck up and die already!

46:51.220 --> 46:52.570
Pay attention!

47:02.280 --> 47:04.780
There's one thing I forgot to mention...

47:04.780 --> 47:08.500
My friend over there is a lot stronger than I am.

47:10.150 --> 47:11.890
What the hell is he talking about?

47:11.890 --> 47:15.750
Blondie couldn't handle him. Isn't that why you stepped up to the plate?

47:23.870 --> 47:28.600
If you beat me, that automatically means that blondie couldn't have lost to me.

47:28.600 --> 47:32.260
You can't lose now, because you have to prove how strong blondie is.

47:33.210 --> 47:36.270
How poetic. This is what a best friend does.

47:36.590 --> 47:38.700
What's wrong? Come at me.

47:38.700 --> 47:41.770
Acting so cocky! You make me puke!

47:46.930 --> 47:51.710
Get up! Kick his ass! What are you doing?!

47:52.090 --> 47:54.170
This is why Itou is so badass.

47:54.170 --> 47:55.480
Don't think you've won!

47:55.480 --> 47:56.950
Your speed has deserted you!

47:56.950 --> 47:58.710
What the hell!

47:58.710 --> 48:00.120
Your punches do nothing!

48:01.510 --> 48:03.080
Goddamn!

48:05.450 --> 48:06.970
Quit swinging wildly!

48:15.990 --> 48:19.650
Stop acting like you've won, you douchebag.

48:23.410 --> 48:27.010
Damn, that hurt. I can feel the ringing in my skull.

48:27.010 --> 48:29.020
Nakano?! You okay, Nakano?!

48:29.020 --> 48:30.330
Nakano!

48:32.290 --> 48:34.010
Let's get out of here, Mitsuhashi.

48:36.270 --> 48:40.980
Man, couldn't you have tried winning it with style?

48:40.980 --> 48:44.210
Unfortunately, my opponent didn't give me much option.

48:44.210 --> 48:45.570
He’s pretty—

48:51.550 --> 48:54.170
C'mon, please stop! He's had enough!

48:54.170 --> 48:54.930
Shut up!

48:57.910 --> 49:02.910
Hey, midget! How pathetic.
You can’t even move, can you?

49:04.870 --> 49:06.610
Say something.

49:06.610 --> 49:08.080
C'mon! Say you're sorry!

49:17.890 --> 49:22.110
This feels like shit. This is why I hate losing...

49:25.140 --> 49:26.110
Hey!

49:32.650 --> 49:34.510
Wh-What the hell are you doing?!

49:35.450 --> 49:39.610
Whaling on a guy who can't even get up... Isn't that cheating?

49:39.610 --> 49:42.180
Are you fucked in the head? Get outta here!

49:42.180 --> 49:43.060
You heard him, dickhead!

49:43.450 --> 49:45.510
I'm afraid I can't do that.

49:45.510 --> 49:47.250
Because...

49:48.200 --> 49:50.530
fighting dirty is my signature move!

50:07.550 --> 50:09.050
So... time to split?

50:09.050 --> 50:09.860
Yeah.

50:11.720 --> 50:14.010
W-Wait...

50:15.580 --> 50:20.320
We didn't ask for your help... Come settle this...

50:20.320 --> 50:23.790
My, my. You've got huge conkers for a little guy.

50:23.790 --> 50:25.170
What should we do, Mitsuhashi?

50:26.670 --> 50:30.250
I dunno. I can't bring myself to care anymore. Let's blow this joint.

50:30.250 --> 50:31.410
Let's do just that.

50:33.030 --> 50:36.250
So that's all for now. Catch you around, Stumpy.

50:37.930 --> 50:40.720
What's with you?! You're limping!

50:40.720 --> 50:41.940
No, I'm not!

50:41.940 --> 50:44.510
Liar. I just saw you stumble.

50:44.830 --> 50:47.110
You're still feeling those hits, aren't you?

50:47.110 --> 50:50.170
Not at all. I'm doing just fine.

50:50.170 --> 50:51.910
Acting tough now, are we?

50:52.490 --> 50:54.930
Those two are fucking weird.

50:57.330 --> 51:00.150
What is it, Nakano? Does it hurt somewhere?

51:00.150 --> 51:01.480
Shut your face.

51:03.710 --> 51:06.390
Seriously... those two are batshit crazy.

51:19.390 --> 51:20.260
Itou.

51:20.260 --> 51:21.350
Yeah?

51:21.350 --> 51:23.050
Kyoto's a nice place.

51:23.050 --> 51:24.290
It sure is.

51:24.290 --> 51:26.870
I'm definitely coming to Kyoto for my honeymoon.

51:26.870 --> 51:28.290
Honeymoon? With who?

51:28.750 --> 51:30.070
Who, you ask?

51:37.060 --> 51:40.230
Look at all those bruises!

51:40.230 --> 51:43.020
You <i>were fighting!</i>

51:43.020 --> 51:43.810
Uh-oh...

51:43.810 --> 51:46.190
I get why Kyou's here, but why Riko?

51:46.190 --> 51:49.770
Ha, I bet you're secretly happy she waited up for you!

51:49.770 --> 51:52.700
Hey! Keep that up and you're cruisin' for a bruisin'!

51:52.700 --> 51:54.540
Do something about it, then!

51:54.540 --> 51:55.790
All right, I will.

51:56.370 --> 52:01.150
Kyouko! He totally broke his promise with you, and started fighting!

52:01.150 --> 52:02.850
You little weasel!

52:02.850 --> 52:05.750
Kyouko!

52:03.810 --> 52:05.750
Stop that, Mitsuhashi!

52:24.510 --> 52:26.170
Tanigawa?

52:26.170 --> 52:26.870
Yes?

52:26.870 --> 52:29.690
Mitsuhashi's pretty late.

52:29.690 --> 52:32.750
Yeah, he's really late.

52:32.750 --> 52:37.170
Maybe he got lost or something. He is a birdbrain, after all.

52:37.170 --> 52:41.670
It's definitely possible. He is a birdbrain, for sure.

52:44.110 --> 52:46.890
But you know what, Tanigawa?

52:46.890 --> 52:48.110
Yes?

52:48.110 --> 52:51.310
The Kyoto landscape is really pretty.

52:51.310 --> 52:54.600
So it is.

53:01.750 --> 53:01.790
And Yet, You're Going to Kyoto!

53:06.520 --> 53:08.630
Let's worry about the future tomorrow.

53:08.630 --> 53:10.940
When tomorrow comes, it'll all work out.

53:14.630 --> 53:16.670
If it doesn't work out, I'll just run away.

53:16.670 --> 53:18.910
If I'm found, I'll make up an excuse.

53:22.610 --> 53:24.650
You and me are friends, partner.

53:24.650 --> 53:26.390
If the going gets tough, the tough say goodbye.

53:30.590 --> 53:32.670
I help you.

53:31.510 --> 53:32.670
We're family.

53:32.670 --> 53:34.630
I like you.

53:46.620 --> 53:48.590
On stressful days, I'll hit you.

53:48.590 --> 53:51.230
Then, I'll say, "I'm sorry," and you'll forgive me.

53:54.500 --> 53:56.040
That cute girl is mine,

53:56.040 --> 53:59.130
but I belong to no one.

54:02.570 --> 54:04.590
We're all brothers and sisters in this world.

54:04.590 --> 54:06.590
When the going gets tough, the tough kick and scream.

54:34.610 --> 54:36.610
You and me are friends, partner.

54:36.610 --> 54:38.600
If the going gets tough, the tough say goodbye.

55:04.680 --> 55:05.470
Until next time!
